-- EXPECT: error: method 'encode' is already registered under trait 'Serializer'; cannot also register under 'Formatter'. Rename one of the methods so each trait has a distinct set of method names, or consolidate the traits if they represent the same concept.
-- EXPECT: error: method 'encode' is already registered under trait 'Serializer'; cannot also register under 'Formatter'. Rename one of the methods so each trait has a distinct set of method names, or consolidate the traits if they represent the same concept.
-- Two unrelated user traits claiming the same method name — the
-- compiler should flag this at the second trait's registration so
-- users don't silently get first-registered-wins dispatch.
trait Serializer:
	pure func encode(value: Self) -> String


trait Formatter:
	pure func encode(value: Self) -> String


func main(args: List[String]) -> Int:
	0
